  "details": "Essentially there are character descriptors that are capable of receiving and using VMC/OSC data to animate an avatar in unity. \n\nI'm suggesting allowing the use of such a descriptor (forgive me if descriptor is the wrong term I'm not proficient in unity) attached directly to an avatar to use for face tracking(mainly face tracking) and possibly body tracking, facial blendshape mapping in realtime. \n\nThis would work similar to how vtubing programs like VSeeFace can also receive OSC/VMC data from external programs and use it to animate a Vtuber avatar. \n\nThis would also make it so that anyone with a Webcam could use it without the need of a VR HMD.\n\nPersonally I've noticed when I play (I do not have an HMD) my character's eyes just always look in weird directions. but more than that I think this would allow a lot of people's characters to appear much more presentable when playing in desktop mode. \n\nbeing able to track eyes, eyebrows and possibly even make use of ARkit blendshapes would allow one to have a much more expressive appearance without the need for an expensive setup and VR headset. \n\nI really do hope this get's implemented and I think it would be amazing for a lot of people playing on desktop without having their characters look awkword all the time",
